---
name: kata

description: |
  EXPERIMENTAL. Installs Kata Containers runtime-rs (containerd shim, Cloud Hypervisor, virtiofsd, guest
  kernel and guest image) and prepares the host for garden's VM runtime mode. Has no processes: containerd starts the
  Kata shim per container. Use together with the garden job properties
    garden.containerd_mode: true
    garden.containerd_vm_runtime: true
    garden.containerd_runtime: /opt/kata/runtime-rs/bin/containerd-shim-kata-v2
  The VM needs hardware virtualization (/dev/kvm), i.e. bare metal or nested virtualization.

templates:
  bin/pre-start.erb: bin/pre-start
  config/10-garden.toml.erb: config/10-garden.toml

packages:
  - kata

properties:
  kata.enabled:
    description: |
      Install and configure Kata on this VM. When false the job does nothing (and removes the configuration it
      installed earlier), so it can be colocated everywhere and switched on per instance group.
    default: false

  kata.rootless:
    description: |
      Run the hypervisor (VMM) as an unprivileged throwaway user per sandbox (Kata runtime-rs). The Kata
      shim and virtiofsd still run as root. Requires /dev/kvm to be group accessible (done by pre-start).
    default: true

  kata.guest_seccomp:
    description: |
      Apply the container's seccomp profile inside the guest VM (Kata's disable_guest_seccomp = false).
      Kata disables guest seccomp by default, which silently drops garden's seccomp profile.
    default: true

  kata.translate_rootfs_ids:
    description: |
      Translate ids on the shared filesystem (virtiofsd --translate-uid/--translate-gid): guest root (0) is the maximus
      user on the host (kata.rootfs_root_host_id) in both directions. Files written by container root then belong to an
      unprivileged host user. Must be used together with garden.containerd_vm_translate_rootfs_ids: true, which makes
      garden create id-shifted root filesystems.
    default: false

  kata.rootfs_root_host_id:
    description: Host uid and gid of container root in id-shifted root filesystems (garden's maximus).
    default: 4294967294

  kata.default_vcpus:
    description: vCPUs of the guest VM at boot (CPU limits of the container are applied on top).
    default: 1

  kata.default_memory_mb:
    description: |
      Guest memory in MiB at boot. Container memory limits are hot-plugged on top. Keep
      garden.containerd_vm_memory_overhead_mb >= this value plus the hypervisor/shim/virtiofsd overhead.
    default: 512

  kata.virtio_fs_extra_args:
    description: |
      Arguments passed to virtiofsd. Replaces Kata's default list, so include the defaults when extending it
      (e.g. --translate-uid / --translate-gid for UID translation).
    default: ["--thread-pool-size=1", "-o", "announce_submounts"]

  kata.virtio_fs_cache:
    description: |
      Guest caching of the shared filesystem (container root filesystems): never, auto or always (Kata's virtio_fs_cache).
      Guest RAM is shared memory on the host (required by vhost-user), so file data cached in the guest stays pinned on
      the host and duplicates the host page cache that virtiofsd reads through. With "never" file data is cached only
      once, in the host page cache, which is reclaimable and shared by sandboxes using the same image layers.
      Cloud Hypervisor with runtime-rs has no DAX window for virtio-fs.
    default: never

  kata.virtio_fs_allow_mmap:
    description: |
      With kata.virtio_fs_cache: never, allow shared writable mmap of files (virtiofsd --allow-mmap), e.g. the JVM's
      hsperfdata. Safe because every sandbox has exclusive access to its shared directory.
    default: true

  kata.reclaim_guest_freed_memory:
    description: |
      Return memory freed in the guest to the host (virtio-balloon free page reporting, Kata's reclaim_guest_freed_memory).
      Without it, guest RAM touched once stays allocated on the host until the VM stops.
    default: true

  kata.debug:
    description: Enable debug logging of the runtime, hypervisor and agent (shows up in syslog as kata[...]).
    default: false

  kata.debug_console:
    description: |
      DEBUG ONLY. Start a root shell in every guest, reachable with `kata-ctl exec <sandbox-id>` (kata-tools).
      Never enable on production cells.
    default: false

  kata.pprof:
    description: DEBUG ONLY. Serve pprof on the shim management socket (/run/vc/sbs/<id>/shim-monitor.sock).
    default: false
